    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="0948" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg852"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2930.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a translation
                    of a communication from the Tsung-li Yamên relating to the neutrality of
                    China.</p>
                <p>It will be noticed that “war vessels of either belligerent can not remain in
                    Chinese ports.” The <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> is the only ship which
                    could be affected by this order, but until some question is made as to her
                    departure I shall take no action unless requested to do so by the admiral. The
                    proclamation cited fixes no time in which vessels are required to leave and is
                    therefore defective.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d723-a1.xml" xpointer="d723-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
